{
    "version": "Antigravity CLI 1.5.15, `agy acp`",
    "source": "Recorded with tee-cli.ts in front of `agy acp` 1.5.15, driven by ADE CORE's ACP backend in supervised mode in a throwaway git folder. The prompt asks for `sleep 20 && echo bg-done` in the background and an immediate end. agy runs it as `run_command` with `IsDaemon` false and `WaitMsBeforeAsync` 500, says \"started\" and sends `usage_update`, but does not answer `session/prompt`: the call stays open while the command runs. When the command completes (`tool_call_update` completed, 17 s later), the model reacts inside the same prompt and only then the one `session/prompt` response ends it with `end_turn`. agy's Stop hook fires twice (`hooks`), after \"started\" with fullyIdle false (the command still runs) and at the real end with fullyIdle true. The same held prompt showed in two more runs not kept as frames: two such commands (each completion woke the model inside the prompt, with a permission each; Stop fired three times with fullyIdle false, false, true, and the response came after the second), and `/schedule` with a 30 s timer (the `schedule` tool call completes when the timer fires, the model acts, then `end_turn` at 45 s). No output came outside a prompt in any of them. Thought chunks are left out, consecutive message chunks are merged into one. `t` is milliseconds from the start, `dir` is `in` for what went to agy.",
